1. INTRODUCTION: THE MISSING ORGAN

1.1 What ST-T1024 Is Today

ST-T1024 replaces stochastic inference with a deterministic pipeline:

· FIS Triage — fuzzy input → crisp domain
· FSM Scheduling — hard real-time, WCET ≤ 800 ns
· Ternary Execution — additions only, no multipliers
· Power Gating — 0V idle, passive cooling
· 0x-AMBIG — refusal instead of hallucination

The system is a mirror. It reflects truth bounded by its ROM. It cannot lie. It cannot drift. It cannot escape.

1.2 What ST-T1024 Is Not

It is not a hand.

It answers "what is the force of gravity?" It does not apply the brake.

It refuses to hallucinate. It does not refuse to act unsafely, because it does not act at all.

1.3 The Thesis of This Paper

The current safety debate assumes a premise that is false:

"Agency and safety are in tension."

This is true for stochastic systems. It is not true for deterministic systems. The tension is a property of the architecture, not of agency itself.

In stochastic systems, agency is the danger. In deterministic systems, agency is the product.

This paper specifies the extension of ST-T1024 to agency, and demonstrates that safety ceases to be a hope and becomes a guarantee over action.

