3.2 The Core Insight

An agent is a policy:

```
State → Action
```

If that policy is ROM-burned, FSM-scheduled, and tile-routed, then the complete set of behaviors the agent can produce is finite and enumerable. You can prove what it will do before you ship it.

This is not a mitigation. It is a category shift.

3.3 What This Enables

· Not "the system won't hallucinate." Already true.
· But "the system won't take unsafe action." New.
· Not "the system is bounded in speech." Already true.
· But "the system is bounded in motion, decision, and consequence." New.

Safety moves from constraint to guarantee. And a guarantee is a product.

